208
00:15:12,134 --> 00:15:28,887
[SPEAKER_01]: When a bhikkhu is completely disenchanted with one thing, completely dispassionate toward it, completely liberated from it, completely sees its delimitations, and completely breaks through its meaning, in this very life, he becomes... he makes an end of suffering.

209
00:15:28,907 --> 00:15:29,748
[SPEAKER_01]: What one thing.

210
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:33,442
[SPEAKER_01]: All beings exist through nutriment.

211
00:15:34,203 --> 00:15:39,887
[SPEAKER_01]: So, understanding that... Understanding the principle of dependence.

212
00:15:40,487 --> 00:15:42,309
[SPEAKER_02]: The principle of depending on a nutrient.

213
00:15:45,992 --> 00:15:47,753
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding the principle, yeah.

214
00:15:48,754 --> 00:15:50,175
[SPEAKER_01]: That's, well, saṅkhara.

215
00:15:50,915 --> 00:15:51,136
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

216
00:15:51,916 --> 00:15:53,137
[SPEAKER_02]: That's a bit, but it's samkhāra.

217
00:15:53,197 --> 00:15:57,901
[SPEAKER_02]: It's in the most concise understanding.

218
00:16:01,217 --> 00:16:03,558
[SPEAKER_01]: The second, second one says a question about two.

219
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,838
[SPEAKER_01]: A consular statement about two, an explanation of two.

220
00:16:07,638 --> 00:16:09,979
